\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Question 1: Identify the Attacking IP Address\
\
Started by pulling all HTTP traffic hitting imreallynotbatman.com to get\
a feel for who was talking to the site:\
\
    index=botsv1 imreallynotbatman.com sourcetype="stream:http"\
\
That returned 22,200 events. Breaking down the source IPs (`c_ip`) showed\
two addresses doing basically all the talking:\
\
- 40.80.148.42 \'97 20,964 events (94.4% of traffic)\
- 23.22.63.114 \'97 1,236 events (5.6%)\
\
40.80.148.42 is clearly the dominant one, but I didn't want to just assume\
"most traffic = the attacker" \'97 busy legit clients can rack up volume too.\
So I pulled the request headers for that IP to see what it was actually\
sending:\
\
    index=botsv1 imreallynotbatman.com sourcetype="stream:http" c_ip="40.80.148.42"\
    | table _time, src_headers | head 5\
\
![Q1 c_ip breakdown](../screenshots/q1-cip-breakdown.png)\
\
\
**Answer:** 40.80.148.42 confirmed by both traffic volume (94.4% of all\
requests) and by direct evidence in the request headers identifying it as\
an unauthorized vulnerability scan.}